    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessEvent" name="No Attacks against Home Router" id="id-24b6b5f9cf7e4f2eb070d850a54f8362">
      <documentation>Hackers are opportunistic. &#xD;
While 80% of routers could be hacked, threat actors typically scan for specific, easily automated entry points—such as routers with remote management interfaces accidentally left open to the public internet, or devices using well-known, hard-coded factory passwords. &#xD;
If a router is vulnerable but hidden behind an ISP’s firewall without its remote management turned on, it is heavily shielded from automated internet-wide compromise attempts</documentation>
      <property key="namespace" value="SABSA"/>
      <property key="stereotype" value="Uncontrollable"/>
      <property key="refCode" value="idUNC.01"/>
      <property key="pTable" value="{&quot;fail&quot;: 0.10, &quot;success&quot;: 0.90}"/>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessEvent" name="No Attack against Home IoT Device" id="id-db529c6c32424c4e8338ba21b6ac22b0">
      <property key="namespace" value="SABSA"/>
      <property key="stereotype" value="Uncontrollable"/>
      <property key="refCode" value="idUNC.04"/>
      <property key="pTable" value="{&quot;fail&quot;: 0.05, &quot;success&quot;: 0.95}"/>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessEvent" name="Vulnerability Management OK (Router)" id="id-4f073383511d4e2781ee8b12b42204a9">
      <documentation>The Home Router itself is the most probable instantiation of Consumer router/CPE firmware is frequently as neglected as the STB's&#xD;
 — default or weak admin credentials, unpatched known CVEs, and (in some markets) no vendor patch cadence at all. &#xD;
A compromised router is an on-path attacker with zero additional effort — it already sits on every packet in and out of the home.&#xD;
&#xD;
------------------------------&#xD;
&#xD;
Proportion of Home Routers Vulnerable to Remote Compromise&#xD;
Studies consistently show that between 60% and 83% of active home routers possess security flaws that expose them to remote compromise. &#xD;
This vulnerability is primarily driven by unpatched firmware, end-of-life hardware, and user configuration neglect. [1, 2, 3, 4, 5] &#xD;
&#xD;
| Study / Source | Estimated Vulnerable Proportion | Primary Cause Identified |&#xD;
|---|---|---|&#xD;
| American Consumer Institute (ACI) | 83% of tested home routers | Outdated firmware and unpatched, known security flaws (averaging 103 vulnerabilities per router). |&#xD;
| Ordr IoT Security Labs | 62% of active routers | Critical vulnerabilities (CVSS 7.0+) natively present in the device firmware. |&#xD;
| Fraunhofer Institute | 100% of tested models | Every single consumer router tested had at least one known unpatched security flaw. |&#xD;
| Which? Consumer Audit | Over 66% (Two-Thirds) | Outdated ISP-provided models that haven't received updates since 2018 or earlier. |&#xD;
| Broadband Genie / IBM | 47% to 81% (via User Behavior) | Natively vulnerable due to consumer habit: 81-86% have never changed the admin password, and 84% have never updated their firmware. |</documentation>
      <property key="namespace" value="SABSA"/>
      <property key="stereotype" value="Uncontrollable"/>
      <property key="refCode" value="idUNC.02"/>
      <property key="pTable" value="{&quot;fail&quot;: 0.70, &quot;success&quot;: 0.30}"/>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessEvent" name="Vulnerability Management OK (IoT)" id="id-3fb27cb3f546449381ccfa2a8c56744b">
      <property key="namespace" value="SABSA"/>
      <property key="stereotype" value="Uncontrollable"/>
      <property key="refCode" value="idUNC.05"/>
      <property key="pTable" value="{&quot;fail&quot;: 0.50, &quot;success&quot;: 0.50}"/>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessEvent" name="No Home IoT Devices" id="id-4399bfd92e2b4ca1a8f0b0bce2dd6cf4">
      <documentation>Excluding Routers &amp; Smart TVs, IoT market pentration by household in EI is:&#xD;
 - Wearables &amp; Health Tech 30%&#xD;
 - Smart Meters &amp; Energy Trackers 14%&#xD;
 - Home Security Cameras, Doorbells &amp; Plugs: 12%</documentation>
      <property key="namespace" value="SABSA"/>
