    <element xsi:type="archimate:Outcome" name="No Compromised IoT Devices" id="id-e119d8c85b4f40aa8f5a5c74d42d7351">
      <documentation>Smart home gadgets (like cheap security cameras, smart plugs, or smart lightbulbs) are notorious for having weak security, unpatched vulnerabilities, or hardcoded passwords. &#xD;
If a hacker infects one of these Internet of Things (IoT) devices with malware (like Mirai or its variants), they can use it as a launchpad to attack your high-value devices (like your personal laptop or IPTV).</documentation>
