    <element xsi:type="archimate:SketchModel" name="2a Quantitative Scenario" id="id-187aa753e92f438ebe4166defd306206" background="0">
      <child xsi:type="archimate:SketchModelSticky" id="id-de1bc700ba9242a9874dd4fa9302d533" name="Sticky" lineColor="#5c5c5c" textAlignment="1" fillColor="#7f7fff" imagePath="images/_KIZfIJ9FEfC6HeFH9O7WBA.png" imagePosition="4">
        <bounds x="6" y="7" width="935" height="526"/>
        <feature name="deriveElementLineColor" value="false"/>
      </child>
      <documentation>This is a reproduction of a 'Click-bait Question ' posed on LinkedIn at about the sametime as I was preparing this presentation.&#xD;
The only possible answer, given the parameters, is 90k and yet offering this result unqualified reveals a fundamental misunderstanding of risk:&#xD;
• The assumption that these risks are Discrete (precise 'spot' values for impact &amp; likelihood - in real-life, these values carry some level of uncertainty;&#xD;
• The assumption that the risks are independent and not triggered by some common cause;&#xD;
i• The lack of any quoted timescale (per day? month? or year?) or the possibility of multiple loss events in that period.</documentation>
    </element>
